# Configure agent tools

```elixir
Mix.install([{:wardrik, "~> 0.1.0-rc.11"}, {:kino, "~> 0.19"}])
```

## Tools

An agent looks up orders, asks before a refund, and reports what paid lookups cost. A capability
returns tools:

```elixir
:ets.new(:orders, [:named_table, :public])
:ets.insert(:orders, [{"A-1", "shipped"}, {"A-2", "delivered"}])

defmodule MyApp.Orders do
  @behaviour WardrikCore.Capability

  alias WardrikCore.Tool

  @impl true
  def tools(_context, _opts) do
    [
      Tool.new!(
        name: "order_status",
        description: "Says where an order is.",
        schema: [order_id: [type: :string, required: true]],
        run: fn %{order_id: id}, _context -> {:ok, status(id)} end,
        annotations: [read_only: true, idempotent: true]
      ),
      Tool.new!(
        name: "refund_order",
        description: "Refunds an order in full.",
        schema: [order_id: [type: :string, required: true]],
        run: fn %{order_id: id}, _context ->
          :ets.insert(:orders, {id, "refunded"})
          {:ok, "Refunded #{id}."}
        end,
        annotations: [destructive: true]
      ),
      Tool.new!(
        name: "track_parcel",
        description: "Asks the carrier where an order's parcel is.",
        schema: [order_id: [type: :string, required: true]],
        run: fn %{order_id: id}, context ->
          # A paid API: report what the call cost.
          {:ok, "#{id} is at the Leeds depot.", WardrikCore.Context.measure(context, :usd, 0.002)}
        end,
        annotations: [read_only: true, open_world: true]
      )
    ]
  end

  def status(id) do
    case :ets.lookup(:orders, id) do
      [{^id, status}] -> status
      [] -> "unknown"
    end
  end
end
```

- `read_only` - changes nothing.
- `idempotent` - safe to repeat. Wardrik repeats one lost in a crash.
- `destructive` - can't be undone.
- `open_world` - reaches outside your systems.

## Defaults by annotation

A policy's `default` decides calls no rule names:

```elixir
policy = Wardrik.Policy.new!(default: [read_only: :allow, destructive: :ask, else: :ask])

for tool <- MyApp.Orders.tools(nil, []) do
  %{tool: tool.name, decision: inspect(Wardrik.Policy.decide(policy, tool.name, annotations: tool.annotations))}
end
|> Kino.DataTable.new(keys: [:tool, :decision])
```

## Start Wardrik

`deepwiki` is for the last section.

```elixir
defmodule MyApp.AllowAll do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Authorizer
  def authorize(_request, _opts), do: :ok
end

defmodule MyApp.Agents do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Resolver

  def resolve(_request, _opts),
    do: {:ok, %Wardrik.Resolved{principal: Wardrik.principal("maria"), servers: %{"deepwiki" => "deepwiki"}}}
end

{:ok, _} =
  Wardrik.start_link(
    name: MyApp.AgentRuntime,
    authorizer: {MyApp.AllowAll, []},
    resolver: {MyApp.Agents, []},
    capabilities: [orders: MyApp.Orders],
    mcp: [deepwiki: [transport: {:streamable_http, url: "https://mcp.deepwiki.com/mcp"}, gated: false]]
  )

scope = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "maria")

{:ok, agent} =
  Wardrik.Agent.define(scope, "agt_support",
    model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5",
    instructions: "You answer questions about Acme's orders. Be brief.",
    tools: ["orders"],
    policy: [default: %{read_only: :allow, destructive: :ask, else: :ask}, budget: [usd: 0.50, per: :day]]
  )
```

## Ask it

Add `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the Secrets panel. The rest costs about two cents.

```elixir
System.put_env("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", System.fetch_env!("LB_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"))

{:ok, reply} = Wardrik.Agent.reply(scope, agent, "Where's order A-1, and where's its parcel?")
reply.text
```

Both tools are read-only, so neither asked.

## A refund asks

```elixir
{:waiting, [refund]} = Wardrik.Agent.reply(scope, agent, "Refund order A-2, please.")
{refund.name, MyApp.Orders.status("A-2")}
```

```elixir
{:ok, _decisions} = Wardrik.Agent.approve(scope, agent: agent, interrupt: refund.id)
{:ok, _reply} = Wardrik.Agent.reply(scope, agent, "What's A-2's status now?")

MyApp.Orders.status("A-2")
```

## What it cost

```elixir
{:ok, page} = Wardrik.Agent.events(scope, agent, types: ["wardrik.tool_call.completed"])

page.events
|> Enum.map(&%{tool: &1.data["tool"]["name"], usd: (&1.data["cost"]["micro_usd"] || 0) / 1_000_000})
|> Kino.DataTable.new(keys: [:tool, :usd], name: "Tool calls")
```

```elixir
{:ok, runs} = Wardrik.Agent.runs(scope, agent)

runs.runs
|> Enum.map(&%{status: &1.status, tool_calls: &1.tool_calls, usd: &1.cost_micro_usd / 1_000_000})
|> Kino.DataTable.new(keys: [:status, :tool_calls, :usd], name: "Runs")
```

## An MCP server

[DeepWiki](https://deepwiki.com) needs no sign-in. Its tools only read, so it started with
`gated: false`:

```elixir
{:ok, wiki} =
  Wardrik.Agent.define(scope, "agt_researcher",
    model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5",
    instructions: "You answer questions about open source projects. Be brief.",
    tools: ["deepwiki/*"],
    policy: [budget: [usd: 0.50, per: :day]]
  )

{:ok, reply} = Wardrik.Agent.reply(scope, wiki, "How does elixir-lang/elixir implement Task.async_stream?")
reply.text
```

Its answers come from outside. After them, any gated call asks a person.

